From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:01:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wine: ARM64EC SEH unwind fixes + JIT alias three-view probe

Covers ml627, ml631-ml639, plus the Steam-era socket and cryptnet/wininet work.

signal_arm64ec.c:
  ml627 - ec_stack_window_step used "frame <= last_frame" and so rejected a
  legitimate frame that had not moved, producing a false unwind failure that
  masked the real c0000005. Now "frame < last_frame" (frame moved backwards).
  ml633 - phase 1 of call_seh_handlers never called ec_stack_window_begin, so
  the window was uninitialised for the first walk. Adds a narrow terminal-root
  predicate with a once-per-walk latch.
  ml631-ml639 - the three-view probe that convicted the guest/pool divergence:
  hash the same 16KB through the guest VA, the pool RX alias and the pool RW
  alias at the fault. poolRX == poolRW with the guest diverging is what proved
  the vm_remap had detached rather than FEX miscompiling.

unixlib.h: ios_jit_alias_probe params. The new enum entry is APPENDED - inserting
one renumbers every later ordinal.

unix/socket.c: per-socket TLS timeline probe for the Steam CM connectivity wall.
cryptnet_main.c, netconnection.c: Steam TLS guards.

(cherry picked from commit 58b9db22108c4ce6e3d67b77b544b2ab8ce46356)
Madeira-commit: 88e0af90c7bce32783404cebfe643534d19f74ca
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-26-wine-latest-rebase.md
Offered-upstream: no
